      "problem": "Which of the following is equivalent to $\\frac{1}{{m}^{2}-9}÷\\frac{2}{m+3}?$",
      "worked_solution": "To compute\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{m}^{2}-9}÷\\frac{2}{m+3},\n$$\n\nwe just need to multiply by the reciprocal of the divisor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{m}^{2}-9}÷\\frac{2}{m+3} & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{{m}^{2}-9}\\cdot \\frac{m+3}{2} & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{(m-3)(m+3)}\\cdot \\frac{m+3}{2} & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{(m-3)\\cancel{(m+3)}}\\cdot \\frac{\\cancel{m+3}}{2} & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{2(m-3)}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
